================================================================================
                                CLOCKER
================================================================================

A lightweight, autonomous, and privacy-focused menu bar time tracker designed
natively for macOS.

Clocker runs discreetly in the macOS menu bar, logging only active work time.
It automatically pauses tracking whenever your Mac goes to sleep, locks the
screen, or turns off the display, and resumes seamlessly upon wake or unlock.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FEATURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Zero-Friction Passive Tracking: Automatically detects lock, sleep, and
  display sleep events via macOS AppKit and Foundation notification centers.
- Native Menu Bar Interface: Built directly on Cocoa NSStatusBar for immediate,
  crystal-clear text display without background dock icons.
- Dedicated Isolated Storage: Organizes weekly structured text reports cleanly
  inside a dedicated Clocker_Reports subfolder.
- Custom Location Picker: Change the reports directory on the fly via standard
  macOS directory chooser dialogs.
- On-Demand Sync: Instantly flush and persist the running session to disk using
  the "Save / Sync Now" menu item (or Cmd + S).
- Autonomous & Standalone: Available as a redistributable, self-contained .dmg
  installer requiring no terminal setup or Python installation.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION & USAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Option A: Direct Download for Non-Developers (.dmg)
---------------------------------------------------
No terminal, Python, or technical knowledge required:

1. Download Clocker-macOS.dmg from the Releases section of this repository.
2. Double-click the downloaded .dmg file to mount it.
3. Drag and drop the Clocker icon into the Applications folder shortcut.
4. Launch Clocker from your Applications folder or Spotlight (Cmd + Space).

IMPORTANT NOTE ON MACOS FIRST LAUNCH (Gatekeeper):
Because Clocker is an unsigned open-source application, macOS may prevent it
from opening on the first try.
To open it: Right-click (or Control-click) Clocker.app in /Applications,
select "Open", and click "Open" in the confirmation dialog. (Or go to
System Settings > Privacy & Security and click "Open Anyway").
This confirmation is only required once.


Option B: Run from Source (Developers)
--------------------------------------
1. Clone the repository:
   git clone https://github.com/klacaroll/clockerGardians.git
   cd clockerGardians

2. Create and activate a virtual environment:
   python3 -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate

3. Install core dependencies:
   pip install --upgrade pip
   pip install pyobjc-framework-Cocoa pyobjc-framework-Quartz

4. Run the application:
   python clock_app.py


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MENU CONTROLS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Today: XXh XXm
  Displays cumulative active time tracked today.

- This week: XXh XXm
  Displays cumulative active time tracked for the current calendar week.

- Save / Sync Now (Shortcut: Cmd + S)
  Flushes active session time directly into the weekly report file.

- Open Reports Folder
  Opens the dedicated Clocker_Reports directory in Finder.

- Change Reports Location...
  Opens a native panel to choose a new destination folder.

- Quit Clocker (Shortcut: Cmd + Q)
  Closes the app and finalizes the open session.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PACKAGING (.DMG)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To build the standalone application bundle and disk image locally:

1. Ensure create-dmg is installed:
   brew install create-dmg

2. Run the automated build script:
   ./build_dmg.sh

The resulting distribution file will be available under:
dist/dmg/Clocker-macOS.dmg


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STORAGE & CONFIGURATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Configuration: Stored in ~/Library/Application Support/Clocker/config.json
- Reports: Stored in Clocker_Reports/ located in your chosen directory
  (defaults to ~/Documents/Clocker_Reports/)
- File Format: Weekly plain text reports named rapport_temps_semaine_<WEEK>_<YEAR>.txt


